speechtext:
Mr. LENNARD;
1.	How many of all ranks of the (a) Royal Canadian Navy; (b) Canadian Army (c) Royal Canadian Air Force, served in the Pacific war theatre before V-J day?
2.	Did all of the above receive Pacific rates of pay? If not, why not?

Mr. BLACK (Yukon);
1.	Was an agreement made between the government of Canada and the government of the United States of America whereby Canadian employees of contractors, where American or Canadian, engaged by the United _ States on projects, including the Alaska highway, in Yukon, were or are covered by the Longshoremen's and Harbour Workers' Compensation Act of the United States, and that no Canadian provincial or federal workmen's compensation laws would apply to such employees in Yukon?
2.	Was an agreement made between the government of Canada and the government of the United States of America whereby Canadian or other civilians suffering injury and incurring damages due to negligence on the part of a member or members of the army of the United States of America in Yukon, Canada, are deprived of their rights to sue the United States of America or the army of the United States of America for damages in the territorial court of Yukon territory, and, if so, what rights, if any, have been given to or conferred on such Canadians in lieu of the rights of which they have been so deprived?
